[sliver] The 0.610 mm strips are the two analytic 0.45 mm bore-mouth eases around the 4.30 mm seat. They guide a tube into the half-pipe and have the full 10 mm bearing length; no Boolean seam is left here. Black-stock insertion and retention are unmeasured.
alternatives: A plain sharp seat removes the ease and changes insertion contact. A larger mouth changes the enclosing arc; a larger seat changes the required tube clearance.
